{"key":"enterprise/T1036.012","id":"T1036.012","name":"Browser Fingerprint","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1036","tactics":["stealth"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may attempt to blend in with legitimate traffic by spoofing browser and system attributes like operating system, system language, platform, user-agent string, resolution, time zone, etc. The HTTP User-Agent request header is a string that lets servers and network peers identify the application, operating system, vendor, and/or version of the requesting user agent. Adversaries may gather this information through System Information…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1036/012","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--afac5dbc-4383-4fb6-9ba6-45b25d49e530","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.707Z","source_object_version":"2.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0082","name":"Network Connection Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0082","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--181a9f8c-c780-4f1f-91a8-edb770e904ba","page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"id":"DC0085","name":"Network Traffic Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0085","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3772e279-27d6-477a-9fe3-c6beb363594c","page":"telemetry/DC0085/"},{"id":"DC0021","name":"OS API Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0021","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9bde2f9d-a695-4344-bfac-f2dce13d121e","page":"telemetry/DC0021/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0898","name":"Detection of Spoofed User-Agent","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0898","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--ad21a251-e824-4368-a04c-8a480ee653cc","relationship_id":"relationship--4f0c1449-c5fb-4d6d-b023-4f59f3fca8b0"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN2029","name":"Analytic 2029","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0898#AN2029","guidance":"Process execution without GUI context (e.g., powershell.exe, wscript.exe) generates HTTP traffic with a spoofed User-Agent mimicking a legitimate browser. No corresponding UI application (e.g., msedge.exe) is active or in parent lineage. The User-Agent deviates from known enterprise baselines or contains spoofed platform indicators. User-Agent strings can be gathered with API calls such as `ShellExecuteW` to open the default browser on a socket to receive an HTTP reply, or by hard coding the User-Agent string for a specific browser.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0898"},{"id":"AN2031","name":"Analytic 2031","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0898#AN2031","guidance":"Detection of HTTP outbound requests with inconsistent or spoofed User-Agent headers from command-line tools (e.g., curl, wget, python requests) following interactive user shells or scheduled jobs outside of normal user session behavior.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0898"},{"id":"AN2032","name":"Analytic 2032","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0898#AN2032","guidance":"Observation of scripted network requests (e.g., using osascript, curl, or python) that include mismatched or spoofed browser User-Agent strings compared to the typical macOS Safari or Chrome baseline, especially when triggered by non-interactive launch agents, login hooks, or background daemons.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0898"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0085","component":"Network Traffic Content","name":"NSM:Flow","channel":"Inbound HTTP POST with suspicious payload size or user-agent","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN2029","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0898#AN2029","vali